-      "text": "Import documents and worksheets Open Setup & builders → Import a document , or use a card’s Import existing action. Documents become editable proposals before anything is saved. Supported files PDF (including clear scans), Word DOCX, Excel XLSX/XLSM, CSV/TSV, TXT, Markdown, and single-page PNG/JPEG/TIFF/WebP images. Use one file up to 12 MB. Save older DOC/XLS files as DOCX/XLSX first. Review the type and worksheet Choose the source and OCR language, or open Use copied document text and paste readable text. Reading the file does not save company records. Review the suggested destination: checklist, maintenance routine, toolbox-talk form, logbook design or inventory. For an inventory workbook, select the item worksheets to combine, review each mapping and location, and choose a new or existing inventory. Other types use one worksheet at a time. Names, source-row counts and suggested types are shown separately. Import another sheet separately if it has a different purpose. Hidden worksheets are named in the extraction notes and skipped. For inventory, choose the header row and map columns. Apply the mapping, then review or edit the tab-separated rows. Unmapped columns remain in the source preview. Blank quantities stay unknown. Box parents must match an explicitly marked box’s asset reference in the selected sheet. Edit the proposal. Checklists and routines show editable sections, checks, instructions, warnings, required tools, stages and answer fields. Open a check’s details to review its source reference, guidance and answer format. Move a proposed check into instructions or warnings when it does not need an answer, or move an instruction into the checks when it does. Toolbox forms need discussion prompts, understanding questions and an acknowledgement declaration. Logbooks use one field per line: Label | type | unit | required | choices separated by semicolons. Supported field types are text, number, date, time and select. Open the complete extracte