ntory-worksheet-overlap"><strong>Review possible overlap across worksheets.</strong> Open <strong>Review possible overlap</strong> to compare exact matching serial numbers (SN) or asset references in included rows from different included worksheets. Each match remains a separate record. Locations and part numbers provide context; matching part numbers or names alone do not identify overlap. Leading zeros and letter case remain significant. These suggestions are not a stock verification or a duplicate verdict. Excluded worksheets and rows are outside this comparison, and items with neither identifier cannot be compared. Pending mapping choices have not changed the displayed rows. Full mapped-row editing can make the original source row unavailable. Use <strong>Inspect items</strong> to review the current worksheet, or <strong>Inspect source row</strong> where a unique original Excel row is available. These controls preserve a completed check and confirmation. Review the original file when source provenance is unavailable. No rows are merged, removed or excluded automatically. If you edit the proposal, use <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving.</p><p id="ui116-inventory-source-headers"><strong>Review source table headers.</strong> Open <strong>Review source table headers</strong> beside the source browser to inspect possible headers in the first 5,000 extracted rows of the current worksheet. Compare each candidate with all 13 recorded last-applied mapping choices. The original column heading and the candidate text at that same column are shown together. Recognized alternative headings, changed positions, missing headings and repeated aliases are suggestions to review against the source. A candidate is not proof of a new table or a correct mapping. Pending choices are not used as an applied mapping, and missing recorded choices remain explicitly unavailable. Full mapped-row edits may differ from the earlier applied source mapping. <strong>Inspect source row</strong> opens the exact extracted row. <strong>Inspect mapped item</strong> is available only when a unique confirmed original Excel row still links to that item. These actions preserve your checked proposal and confirmation. This view does not combine tables, change the header or mapping, remove rows, or estimate table boundaries. Use the existing header chooser and Apply controls for deliberate mapping changes, then check the draft again. No candidates does not prove the worksheet has one consistent layout; review the complete file for merged, adjacent or unrecognized tables.</p></article>
