ows its current mapping status and row choices. The summary names included worksheets with pending mapping and separates missing-name or unavailable-choice advice. <strong>All worksheets</strong>, <strong>Included</strong> and <strong>Needs mapping</strong> only filter the cards on screen; they do not add or exclude worksheets, switch the worksheet being inspected, or change a completed check and confirmation. Needs mapping can show excluded worksheets too. Their advice does not require adding them to the import. Use <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> to inspect a specific worksheet. Apply or restore pending mappings on included worksheets before checking again. A missing source name column is mapping advice; manually edited rows still need comparison with the source and a fresh check. An older draft without a recorded applied mapping remains explicitly unavailable for restoration.</p><p id="ui115-inventory-worksheet-overlap"><strong>Review possible overlap across worksheets.</strong> Open <strong>Review possible overlap</strong> to compare exact matching serial numbers (SN) or asset references in included rows from different included worksheets. Each match remains a separate record. Locations and part numbers provide context; matching part numbers or names alone do not identify overlap. Leading zeros and letter case remain significant. These suggestions are not a stock verification or a duplicate verdict. Excluded worksheets and rows are outside this comparison, and items with neither identifier cannot be compared. Pending mapping choices have not changed the displayed rows. Full mapped-row editing can make the original source row unavailable. Use <strong>Inspect items</strong> to review the current worksheet, or <strong>Inspect source row</strong> where a unique original Excel row is available. These controls preserve a completed check and confirmation. Review the original file when source provenance is unavailable. No rows are merged, removed or excluded 