 <html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" name="viewport"/><title>Import documents and worksheets | Wavelink Help</title><link href="../../../app/static/icon.ico" rel="icon"/><link href="../../../app/static/help.css?v=1.34.10" rel="stylesheet"/></head><body class="topic-page"><header class="masthead"><div class="wrap"><div class="brand"><img alt="Wavelink by AJ Offshore Solutions" src="../../../app/static/icon-192.png"/><span>WAVELINK / AJ OFFSHORE SOLUTIONS · USER HELP 1.34.8</span></div><div class="actions"><a href="../../../START_HERE.html">Full user guide</a><a href="../Wavelink_User_Guide.pdf">Printable guide (PDF)</a><a href="../examples.html">Example checklists</a></div></div></header><main class="wrap layout"><nav aria-label="Help topics" class="nav"><a href="generaltasks.html">General-purpose Tasks</a><details><summary>Browse help topics</summary><a href="start.html">Get started</a><a href="navigation.html">Find your workspace</a><a href="savestatus.html">Connection &amp; saves</a><a href="network.html">Choose the hub network address</a><a href="dashboard.html">Use the Operations dashboard</a><a href="projects.html">Choose and manage projects</a><a href="storage.html">Choose application and data folders</a><a href="users.html">Manage user accounts</a><a href="daily.html">Complete a checklist</a><a href="builder.html">Build a checklist step by step</a><a href="create.html">Build a checklist type</a><a href="document.html">Checklist document details</a><a href="originals.html">Keep and link original documents</a><a href="illustrations.html">Add introductions and pictures</a><a href="evidence.html">Record photographic evidence</a><a href="evidencereview.html">Review and keep photo evidence</a><a aria-current="page" href="documentimport.html">Import a prepared work instruction</a><a href="types.html">Organise and delete types</a><a href="departments.html">Manage departments</a><a href="approvals.html">Set up item approval</a><a href="live.html">Use an optional live checklist</a><a href="records.html">Manage checklist records</a><a href="transfers.html">Export and import project workspaces</a><a href="phones.html">Phone access and installation</a><a href="https.html">Secure connections</a><a href="backups.html">Back up and update</a><a href="uninstall.html">Uninstall Wavelink</a><a href="inventory.html">Find and move inventory</a><a href="inventorybuilder.html">Build an inventory</a><a href="stocktake.html">Stock verification</a><a href="inventorytransfer.html">Import and export inventory</a><a href="toolbox.html">Conduct a toolbox talk</a><a href="toolboxbuilder.html">Build and import toolbox forms</a><a href="toolboxguests.html">Add guests and collect acknowledgements</a><a href="support.html">Help and support</a><a href="logs.html">Create and use logbooks</a><a href="logimport.html">Import a multi-tab operations workbook</a><a href="logreferences.html">Review equipment and illustrated references</a><a href="logexports.html">Export and transfer logbooks</a><a href="offsets.html">Record lever arms and angular offsets</a><a href="permissions.html">Set user permissions</a><a href="logbuilder.html">Build a logbook step by step</a><a href="assignments.html">Assign issues and follow alerts</a><a href="datetime.html">Choose dates and times</a><a href="tasks.html">Assign private verification tasks</a><a href="departmentheads.html">Designate department heads</a><a href="maintenance.html">Record maintenance work</a><a href="maintenancebuilder.html">Build a maintenance routine</a><a href="containers.html">Keep items inside boxes and kits</a><a href="logwindows.html">Expand a log and keep another window open</a><a href="certificates.html">Keep certificates with equipment</a><a href="assetdetails.html">Open asset details and photographs</a><a href="assetlabels.html">Print and scan inventory QR labels</a><a href="assetcalendar.html">Use the linked project calendar</a><a href="lowstock.html">Set low-stock alerts</a><a href="qrverification.html">Scan labels during stock verification</a><a href="fleet.html">Manage vessels and shore bases</a><a href="fleetaccess.html">Set vessel-only access</a><a href="manifests.html">Dispatch and receive with manifests</a><a href="receiving.html">Receive equipment and record final placement</a><a href="itemjourney.html">Follow an item’s journey</a><a href="vessellogs.html">Use vessel-specific logbooks</a><a href="vessellogaccess.html">Set vessel log permissions</a><a href="browseradmin.html">Browser administration and navigation</a><a href="accessreview.html">Review effective access and sensitive backups</a><a href="browsertemplates.html">Browser checklist and maintenance authoring</a><a href="browsertoolbox.html">Browser toolbox-talk form authoring</a><a href="browserlogs.html">Design logbooks in the browser</a></details><a href="handovers.html">Handovers: private drafts and revisions</a><a href="handovercontinuity.html">Prepare handovers &amp; current recipients</a></nav><div class="content"><section class="chapter" data-topic="documentimport" id="documentimport"><p class="kicker">User instructions</p><h1>Import documents and worksheets</h1><p class="subtitle">Review an editable browser proposal or a prepared native package</p><h2>Browser document import</h2>
 <p>In the browser, open <strong>Setup &amp; builders → Import a document</strong> to read a supported PDF, Word document, spreadsheet, image or text file into an editable proposal. Reading the source does not save a company record.</p>
 <ol><li>Review the suggested destination: checklist, maintenance routine, toolbox-talk form, logbook design or inventory. Each destination follows its current builder permissions.</li><li>For inventory, choose the item worksheets, review each header and column mapping, then choose the locations and a new or permitted existing inventory. Other destinations use one worksheet at a time.</li><li>Review the proposed sections, instructions, required tools, checks, stages and answer fields. Toolbox forms use discussion prompts, understanding questions, a supervisor instruction and declaration. Source answers, names and signatures never become completed work.</li><li>Compare <strong>Review source interpretation</strong>, extraction notes and the complete source with the original document. Correct the proposal before checking it.</li><li>Select <strong>Check edited draft</strong>, review the summary and confirm your review. Save the unpublished definition or reviewed inventory items, then open the exact saved result. If a save response is lost, preserve the proposal and use <strong>Retry unchanged request</strong>.</li></ol>
-<p>The original file bytes are not uploaded to Original files by this flow. Keep the source copy; add it separately there if needed and permitted. The importer does not record stock verification, movement, signatures or procedure approval.</p><h2>Native Windows package import (separate workflow)</h2><ol><li>Open the intended project. In <strong>Checklist Editor → Document tools → Import checklist…</strong>, select a supplied <strong>.ajcheck</strong> package. Review its title, item count, pictures and outstanding review points.</li><li>Confirm <strong>Import as a new draft</strong>. The new type is unpublished and does not replace any existing template or completed record.</li><li>Use <strong>Preview checklist</strong>, <strong>Introduction &amp; pictures</strong> and each item editor to compare the text, photo placement and stage mapping with the controlled source. Open <strong>Original checklist annotations</strong> in the preview when earlier source notes are present.</li><li>Open <strong>Import review</strong>. Record what was checked or corrected before marking a point reviewed and resolved. Resolve every outstanding point before publication.</li><li>Review the code, source procedure reference and local reviewer assignments. Save the draft, publish after responsible local review and test a practice record before operational use.</li></ol><p>The native Checklist Editor imports prepared .ajcheck packages. To read a Word or PDF source into an editable proposal, use Setup &amp; builders → Import a document and compare the proposal with the controlled source before saving. A prepared adaptation can retain the source’s introductory material, numbered steps and pictures. Source revision and Wavelink publication revision are separate.</p><aside class="note">Do not infer approval from a filename, a signature-like name or an app publication. Keep source copyright and attribution, resolve contradictory document status and use the current vessel/project procedure. A checkbox is not a physical hold point, crane interlock or permission to start work.</aside><p>For reusable sharing, choose <strong>Export checklist…</strong> in the editor. This exports the current editable draft with its pictures but no completed work or signatures. Imported named-person approvals must be assigned to a local reviewer. Keep the source document available for comparison.</p><p>To keep the original Word/PDF alongside the adapted checklist, add it separately to <strong>Original documents</strong>, then link the saved revision in the draft. Importing the prepared .ajcheck does not automatically attach your computer’s source file.</p><div class="topic-links"><a href="evidencereview.html">← Review and keep photo evidence</a><a href="types.html">Organise and delete types →</a></div></section><section class="chapter" id="ui106-source-interpretation"><h2>Review how the source was interpreted</h2><p>In <strong>Setup &amp; builders → Import a document</strong>, open <strong>Review source interpretation</strong> to compare uncertain passages with their available source locations. A Review control focuses the existing editor; it does not change wording or approve the draft. Original Excel rows and PDF page/printed-row labels are distinct from extracted table positions, blocks and text lines.</p><p>Correct instructions, warnings, tools, answer types and before/after stages in the proposal. Printed Yes/No, Sim/Não and Pass/Fail labels may become choices; source ticks, historical answers and signatures never become completed work. An unspecified Status column still needs review. The panel records the original extraction and does not mark its points resolved merely because wording changed.</p><p>A toolbox definition uses discussion prompts rather than separate checklist instruction/tool fields. Use <strong>Add instructions and tools to discussion</strong> to include their source wording in editable groups, then check the changed draft again. Native prompt limits apply; guidance is not silently shortened. Review the understanding questions, supervisor instruction and acknowledgement declaration before saving an unpublished form.</p><p>Switching a worksheet shows that worksheet’s review points. Compare the complete source for missing material, and retain your original file. No import proves that every passage or layout has been recognized.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui107-boxes-and-contents"><h2>Review boxes and their contents before import</h2><p>After mapping an inventory worksheet, open <strong>Boxes and contents</strong>. Review each included row's asset/tag reference, explicit box flag, parent box reference and expected quantity. Searching, paging and opening this view do not change the checked proposal. Editing a field requires checking the changed draft again.</p><p>A parent must be an included, explicitly marked box with a unique asset/tag reference in the <strong>same worksheet</strong>. Use its exact reference, including leading zeros and punctuation, or choose <strong>No container</strong> deliberately. A name, serial number, part number, indentation or the word BOX does not establish a relationship. References across worksheets or to boxes already in the destination inventory are not resolved during this import.</p><p>Review missing or excluded parents, duplicate references, self-links, cycles and excessive depth. A box describes one container; use an expected quantity of one or leave it Unknown when appropriate. Ordinary stock can have zero or another valid expected quantity. No imported quantity is a completed stock verification.</p><p>Contained rows inherit their top box's effective location. The checked import summary uses that location before saving, and a differing mapped location is retained in Notes. Review this together with worksheet locations. A location note records the reviewed mapping; it is not proof of a physical move.</p><p>Explicit parent and box-flag headers help suggest inventory. Unqualified Box/Container ID or reference headers can identify the row itself or its parent, so map them deliberately as an asset/tag or parent reference. Unmapped source columns remain available as source notes.</p><p>Field edits keep full mapped row order, original row references when available and item choices. Reapplying a mapping replaces the mapped values and these corrections; editing the complete table can reset source references and choices. Review the visible notice before continuing. Pending or uncertain saves must retain their unchanged retry request.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui108-table-source-review"><h2>Review table instructions and sections</h2><p>Clearly labelled descriptions, instructions and required tools can be retained from label-and-value tables or labelled rows inside a check table. Before and after headings and changed printed column headers help organize the following checks. Read <strong>Review source interpretation</strong> and compare the proposed wording, stages and answer fields with the source before saving.</p><p>A printed response definition can describe a new answer field; a completed response, signature or name is not a new answer. Unclear tables still require manual correction. For a toolbox talk, deliberately copy retained instructions and tools into discussion prompts when appropriate.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui108-inventory-source-review"><h2>Review source rows and header choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, use <strong>Needs source review</strong> to inspect rows that resemble repeated headers, headings, summaries, instructions or footers. The advice describes the original extracted source. Rows remain included until you deliberately exclude them. Items can legitimately be called Total or Instructions; compare their identifiers and expected quantities with the source.</p><p>The header selector includes the first 250 extracted nonempty rows. Open <strong>Find header row</strong> to search and page through any extracted row, compare its preview, and choose the actual column header. Original Excel row labels appear only when the extractor proves them. Review any notice about rows before the selected header or other header candidates. Changing the header requires applying the mapping and checking the changed proposal again.</p><p>Editing the complete raw table clears source-row advice and provenance when they can no longer be established. Field corrections keep their original-source references, but do not turn the original advice into a statement about the corrected item. Source Counted columns remain Notes; the app performs stock verification.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-log-definitions"><h2>Review printed log column headings</h2><p>Log proposals use supported printed column headings rather than completed metadata rows. Review the date, time, event and physical reading fields against the actual source. Common unambiguous physical headings can propose numeric fields with their printed units; a previous measurement, vessel name or signature does not become a new field label or observation.</p><p>If later printed headers change the table layout, compare the located advice in <strong>Review source interpretation</strong> with the source and edit the log fields. The proposal retains the first supported schema for that source table; separate or correct other layouts deliberately. Exact repeated headers do not add duplicate fields. Selected worksheets retain their own names. Unclear headings still need manual correction.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-toolbox-discussion-tables"><h2>Review Toolbox discussion tables</h2><p>Explicit <strong>Topic</strong> and <strong>Discussion points</strong> table columns can supply reusable discussion prompts. Compare the retained wording and located source review with the document. Completed answer, signature and attendee columns are excluded from new prompts and responses.</p><p>The existing Toolbox form still requires deliberately reviewed understanding questions and a declaration. Importing a definition does not sign, complete or approve a meeting. Labelled instructions, tools and supervisor guidance remain available; use the existing instruction/tool copy action when those blocks should become discussion prompts.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-inventory-item-corrections"><h2>Correct one imported item without resetting choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, open <strong>Edit item</strong> to correct that row's <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Serial number (SN)</strong> or <strong>Part number (PN)</strong>. Apply a real change, then <strong>Check</strong> the proposal again. Cancel or an unchanged Apply retains the existing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships.</p><p>Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains.</p></section><footer class="topic-footer"><strong>Wavelink · AJ Offshore Solutions</strong><p>Product support: <a href="mailto:support@mywavelink.com">support@mywavelink.com</a></p><p>Use your organisation’s approved procedures. This guide does not authorise operations.</p></footer></div><p id="ui111-inventory-review-safeguards"><strong>Keep corrections while reviewing worksheets.</strong> Switching <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> only changes the worksheet you are inspecting. A completed check, its import overview and your confirmation stay available. Changing included sheets, locations, destination or item fields still requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again. Before <strong>Apply mapping</strong> replaces manually corrected names, SN/PN, quantities or box relationships, review the warning for that worksheet. Cancel keeps the corrected rows. Confirm replaces corrections for that worksheet with mapped source values and requires another check. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal.</p><p id="ui112-inventory-review-navigation"><strong>Navigate the inventory review.</strong> <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> and each worksheet’s <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> button change only the sheet on screen. <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping.</p><p id="ui113-inventory-mapping-recovery"><strong>Undo pending mapping choices without replacing corrected rows.</strong> <strong>Restore last applied mapping</strong> restores the recorded header and column choices for the worksheet you are inspecting. Current item edits, full Notes, row exclusions, source references and box relationships stay in place. The pending changes show which destination fields or header were changed. Restoration does not apply source values to the rows and requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving. <strong>Apply mapping to rows</strong> still replaces mapped values and asks before replacing deliberate corrections. The restore action is unavailable if this draft has no recorded last-applied mapping; older drafts are not guessed from their item rows. Busy or uncertain saves remain locked; resolve an uncertain result with the unchanged retry.</p><p id="ui114-inventory-worksheet-overview"><strong>Review mapping across worksheets.</strong> Each card in <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows its current mapping status and row choices. The summary names included worksheets with pending mapping and separates missing-name or unavailable-choice advice. <strong>All worksheets</strong>, <strong>Included</strong> and <strong>Needs mapping</strong> only filter the cards on screen; they do not add or exclude worksheets, switch the worksheet being inspected, or change a completed check and confirmation. Needs mapping can show excluded worksheets too. Their advice does not require adding them to the import. Use <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> to inspect a specific worksheet. Apply or restore pending mappings on included worksheets before checking again. A missing source name column is mapping advice; manually edited rows still need comparison with the source and a fresh check. An older draft without a recorded applied mapping remains explicitly unavailable for restoration.</p><p id="ui115-inventory-worksheet-overlap"><strong>Review possible overlap across worksheets.</strong> Open <strong>Review possible overlap</strong> to compare exact matching serial numbers (SN) or asset references in included rows from different included worksheets. Each match remains a separate record. Locations and part numbers provide context; matching part numbers or names alone do not identify overlap. Leading zeros and letter case remain significant. These suggestions are not a stock verification or a duplicate verdict. Excluded worksheets and rows are outside this comparison, and items with neither identifier cannot be compared. Pending mapping choices have not changed the displayed rows. Full mapped-row editing can make the original source row unavailable. Use <strong>Inspect items</strong> to review the current worksheet, or <strong>Inspect source row</strong> where a unique original Excel row is available. These controls preserve a completed check and confirmation. Review the original file when source provenance is unavailable. No rows are merged, removed or excluded automatically. If you edit the proposal, use <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving.</p></main></body></html>+<p>The original file bytes are not uploaded to Original files by this flow. Keep the source copy; add it separately there if needed and permitted. The importer does not record stock verification, movement, signatures or procedure approval.</p><h2>Native Windows package import (separate workflow)</h2><ol><li>Open the intended project. In <strong>Checklist Editor → Document tools → Import checklist…</strong>, select a supplied <strong>.ajcheck</strong> package. Review its title, item count, pictures and outstanding review points.</li><li>Confirm <strong>Import as a new draft</strong>. The new type is unpublished and does not replace any existing template or completed record.</li><li>Use <strong>Preview checklist</strong>, <strong>Introduction &amp; pictures</strong> and each item editor to compare the text, photo placement and stage mapping with the controlled source. Open <strong>Original checklist annotations</strong> in the preview when earlier source notes are present.</li><li>Open <strong>Import review</strong>. Record what was checked or corrected before marking a point reviewed and resolved. Resolve every outstanding point before publication.</li><li>Review the code, source procedure reference and local reviewer assignments. Save the draft, publish after responsible local review and test a practice record before operational use.</li></ol><p>The native Checklist Editor imports prepared .ajcheck packages. To read a Word or PDF source into an editable proposal, use Setup &amp; builders → Import a document and compare the proposal with the controlled