mn still needs review. The panel records the original extraction and does not mark its points resolved merely because wording changed.</p><p>A toolbox definition uses discussion prompts rather than separate checklist instruction/tool fields. Use <strong>Add instructions and tools to discussion</strong> to include their source wording in editable groups, then check the changed draft again. Native prompt limits apply; guidance is not silently shortened. Review the understanding questions, supervisor instruction and acknowledgement declaration before saving an unpublished form.</p><p>Switching a worksheet shows that worksheet’s review points. Compare the complete source for missing material, and retain your original file. No import proves that every passage or layout has been recognized.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui107-boxes-and-contents"><h2>Review boxes and their contents before import</h2><p>After mapping an inventory worksheet, open <strong>Boxes and contents</strong>. Review each included row's asset/tag reference, explicit box flag, parent box reference and expected quantity. Searching, paging and opening this view do not change the checked proposal. Editing a field requires checking the changed draft again.</p><p>A parent must be an included, explicitly marked box with a unique asset/tag reference in the <strong>same worksheet</strong>. Use its exact reference, including leading zeros and punctuation, or choose <strong>No container</strong> deliberately. A name, serial number, part number, indentation or the word BOX does not establish a relationship. References across worksheets or to boxes already in the destination inventory are not resolved during this import.</p><p>Review missing or excluded parents, duplicate references, self-links, cycles and excessive depth. A box describes one container; use an expected quantity of one or leave it Unknown when appropriate. Ordinary stock can have zero or another valid expected quantity. No imported quantity is a completed stock verification.</p><p>Contained rows inherit their top box's effective location. The checked import summary uses that location before saving, and a differing mapped location is retained in Notes. Review this together with worksheet locations. A location note records the reviewed mapping; it is not proof of a physical move.</p><p>Explicit parent and box-flag headers help suggest inventory. Unqualified Box/Container ID or reference headers can identify the row itself or its parent, so map them deliberately as an asset/tag or parent reference. Unmapped source columns remain available as source notes.</p><p>Field edits keep full mapped row order, original row references when available and item choices. Reapplying a mapping replaces the mapped values and these corrections; editing the complete table can reset source references and choices. Review the visible notice before continuing. Pending or uncertain saves must retain their unchanged retry request.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui108-table-source-review"><h2>Review table instructions and sections</h2><p>Clearly labelled descriptions, instructions and required tools can be retained from label-and-value tables or labelled rows inside a check table. Before and after headings and changed printed column headers help organize the following checks. Read <strong>Review source interpretation</strong> and compare the proposed wording, stages and answer fields with the source before saving.</p><p>A printed response definition can describe a new answer field; a completed response, signature or name is not a new answer. Unclear tables still require manual correction. For a toolbox talk, deliberately copy retained instructions and tools into discussion prompts when appropriate.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui108-inventory-source-review"><h2>Review source rows and header choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, use <strong>Needs source review</strong> to inspect rows that resemble repeated headers, headings, summaries, instructions or footers. The advice describes the original extracted source. Rows remain included until you deliberately exclude them. Items can legitimately be called Total or Instructions; compare their identifiers and expected quantities with the source.</p><p>The header selector includes the first 250 extracted nonempty rows. Open <strong>Find header row</strong> to search and page through any extracted row, compare its preview, and choose the actual column header. Original Excel row labels appear only when the extractor proves them. Review any notice about rows before the selected header or other header candidates. Changing the header requires applying the mapping and checking the changed proposal again.</p><p>Editing the complete raw table clears source-row advice and provenance when they can no longer be established. Field corrections keep their original-source references, but do not turn the original advice into a statement about the corrected item. Source Counted columns remain Notes; the app performs stock verification.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-log-definitions"><h2>Review printed log column headings</h2><p>Log proposals use supported printed column headings rather than completed metadata rows. Review the date, time, event and physical reading fields against the actual source. Common unambiguous physical headings can propose numeric fields with their printed units; a previous measurement, vessel name or signature does not become a new field label or observation.</p><p>If later printed headers change the table layout, compare the located advice in <strong>Review source interpretation</strong> with the source and edit the log fields. The proposal retains the first supported schema for that source table; separate or correct other layouts deliberately. Exact repeated headers do not add duplicate fields. Selected worksheets retain their own names. Unclear headings still need manual correction.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-toolbox-discussion-tables"><h2>Review Toolbox discussion tables</h2><p>Explicit <strong>Topic</strong> and <strong>Discussion points</strong> table columns can supply reusable discussion prompts. Compare the retained wording and located source review with the document. Completed answer, signature and attendee columns are excluded from new prompts and responses.</p><p>The existing Toolbox form still requires deliberately reviewed understanding questions and a declaration. Importing a definition does not sign, complete or approve a meeting. Labelled instructions, tools and supervisor guidance remain available; use the existing instruction/tool copy action when those blocks should become discussion prompts.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-inventory-item-corrections"><h2>Correct one imported item without resetting choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, open <strong>Edit item</strong> to correct that row's <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Serial number (SN)</strong> or <strong>Part number (PN)</strong>. Apply a real change, then <strong>Check</strong> the proposal again. Cancel or an unchanged Apply retains the existing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships.</p><p>Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains.</p></section><footer class="topic-footer"><strong>Wavelink · AJ Offshore Solutions</strong><p>Product support: <a href="mailto:support@mywavelink.com">support@mywavelink.com</a></p><p>Use your organisation’s approved procedures. This guide does not authorise operations.</p></footer></div><p id="ui111-inventory-review-safeguards"><strong>Keep corrections while reviewing worksheets.</strong> Switching <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> only changes the worksheet you are inspecting. A completed check, its import overview and your confirmation stay available. Changing included sheets, locations, destination or item fields still requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again. Before <strong>Apply mapping</strong> replaces manually corrected names, SN/PN, quantities or box relationships, review the warning for that worksheet. Cancel keeps the corrected rows. Confirm replaces corrections for that worksheet with mapped source values and requires another check. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal.</p><p id="ui112-inventory-review-navigation"><strong>Navigate the inventory review.</strong> <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> and each worksheet’s <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> button change only the sheet on screen. <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping.</p><p id="ui113-inventory-mapping-recovery"><strong>Undo pending mapping choices without replacing corrected rows.</strong> <strong>Restore last applied mapping</strong> restores the recorded header and column choices for the worksheet you are inspecting. Current item edits, full Notes, row exclusions, source references and box relationships stay in place. The pending changes show which destination fields or header were changed. Restoration does not apply source values to the rows and requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving. <strong>Apply mapping to rows</strong> still replaces mapped values and asks before replacing deliberate corrections. The restore action is unavailable if this draft has no recorded last-applied mapping; older drafts are not guessed from their item rows. Busy or uncertain saves remain locked; resolve an uncertain result with the unchanged retry.</p><p id="ui114-inventory-worksheet-overview"><strong>Review mapping across worksheets.</strong> Each card in <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows its current mapping status and row choices. The summary names included worksheets with pending mapping and separates missing-name or unavailable-choice advice. <strong>All worksheets</strong>, <strong>Included</strong> and <strong>Needs mapping</strong> only filter the cards on screen; they do not add or exclude worksheets, switch the worksheet being inspected, or change a completed check and confirmation. Needs mapping can show excluded worksheets too. Their advice does not require adding them to the import. Use <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> to inspect a specific worksheet. Apply or restore pending mappings on included worksheets before checking again. A missing source name column is mapping advice; manually edited rows still need comparison with the source and a fresh check. An older draft without a recorded applied mapping remains explicitly unavailable for restoration.</p><p id="ui115-inventory-worksheet-overlap"><strong>Review possible overlap across worksheets.</strong> Open <strong>Review possible overlap</strong> to compare exact matching serial numbers (SN) or asset references in included rows from different included worksheets. Each match remains a separate record. Locations and part numbers provide context; matching part numbers or names alone do not identify overlap. Leading zeros and letter case remain significant. These suggestions are not a stock verification or a duplicate verdict. Excluded worksheets and rows are outside this comparison, and items with neither identifier cannot be compared. Pending mapping choices have not changed the displayed rows. Full mapped-row editing can make the original source row unavailable. Use <strong>Inspect items</strong> to review the current worksheet, or <strong>Inspect source row</strong> where a unique original Excel row is available. These controls preserve a completed check and confirmation. Review the original file when source provenance is unavailable. No rows are merged, removed or excluded automatically. If you edit the proposal, use <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving.</p><p id="ui116-inventory-source-headers"><strong>Review source table headers.</strong> Open <strong>Review source table headers</strong> beside the source browser to inspect possible headers in the first 5,000 extracted rows of the current worksheet. Compare each candidate with all 13 recorded last-applied mapping choices. The original column heading and the candidate text at that same column are shown together. Recognized alternative headings, changed positions, missing headings and repeated aliases are suggestions to review against the source. A candidate is not proof of a new table or a correct mapping. Pending choices are not used as an applied mapping, and missing recorded choices remain explicitly unavailable. Full mapped-row edits may differ from the earlier applied source mapping. <strong>Inspect source row</strong> opens the exact extracted row. <strong>Inspect mapped item</strong> is available only when a unique confirmed original Excel row still links to that item. These actions preserve your checked proposal and confirmation. This view does not combine tables, change the header or mapping, remove rows, or estimate table boundaries. Use the existing header chooser and Apply controls for deliberate mapping changes, then check the draft again. No candidates does not prove the worksheet has one consistent layout; review the complete file for merged, adjacent or unrecognized tables.</p></main></body></html>--- a/docs/user/topics/inventorybuilder.html
