 <html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" name="viewport"/><title>Build an inventory | Wavelink Help</title><link href="../../../app/static/icon.ico" rel="icon"/><link href="../../../app/static/help.css?v=1.34.10" rel="stylesheet"/></head><body class="topic-page"><header class="masthead"><div class="wrap"><div class="brand"><img alt="Wavelink by AJ Offshore Solutions" src="../../../app/static/icon-192.png"/><span>WAVELINK / AJ OFFSHORE SOLUTIONS · USER HELP 1.34.8</span></div><div class="actions"><a href="../../../START_HERE.html">Full user guide</a><a href="../Wavelink_User_Guide.pdf">Printable guide (PDF)</a><a href="../examples.html">Example checklists</a></div></div></header><main class="wrap layout"><nav aria-label="Help topics" class="nav"><a href="generaltasks.html">General-purpose Tasks</a><details><summary>Browse help topics</summary><a href="start.html">Get started</a><a href="navigation.html">Find your workspace</a><a href="savestatus.html">Connection &amp; saves</a><a href="network.html">Choose the hub network address</a><a href="dashboard.html">Use the Operations dashboard</a><a href="projects.html">Choose and manage projects</a><a href="storage.html">Choose application and data folders</a><a href="users.html">Manage user accounts</a><a href="daily.html">Complete a checklist</a><a href="builder.html">Build a checklist step by step</a><a href="create.html">Build a checklist type</a><a href="document.html">Checklist document details</a><a href="originals.html">Keep and link original documents</a><a href="illustrations.html">Add introductions and pictures</a><a href="evidence.html">Record photographic evidence</a><a href="evidencereview.html">Review and keep photo evidence</a><a href="documentimport.html">Import a prepared work instruction</a><a href="types.html">Organise and delete types</a><a href="departments.html">Manage departments</a><a href="approvals.html">Set up item approval</a><a href="live.html">Use an optional live checklist</a><a href="records.html">Manage checklist records</a><a href="transfers.html">Export and import project workspaces</a><a href="phones.html">Phone access and installation</a><a href="https.html">Secure connections</a><a href="backups.html">Back up and update</a><a href="uninstall.html">Uninstall Wavelink</a><a href="inventory.html">Find and move inventory</a><a aria-current="page" href="inventorybuilder.html">Build an inventory</a><a href="stocktake.html">Stock verification</a><a href="inventorytransfer.html">Import and export inventory</a><a href="toolbox.html">Conduct a toolbox talk</a><a href="toolboxbuilder.html">Build and import toolbox forms</a><a href="toolboxguests.html">Add guests and collect acknowledgements</a><a href="support.html">Help and support</a><a href="logs.html">Create and use logbooks</a><a href="logimport.html">Import a multi-tab operations workbook</a><a href="logreferences.html">Review equipment and illustrated references</a><a href="logexports.html">Export and transfer logbooks</a><a href="offsets.html">Record lever arms and angular offsets</a><a href="permissions.html">Set user permissions</a><a href="logbuilder.html">Build a logbook step by step</a><a href="assignments.html">Assign issues and follow alerts</a><a href="datetime.html">Choose dates and times</a><a href="tasks.html">Assign private verification tasks</a><a href="departmentheads.html">Designate department heads</a><a href="maintenance.html">Record maintenance work</a><a href="maintenancebuilder.html">Build a maintenance routine</a><a href="containers.html">Keep items inside boxes and kits</a><a href="logwindows.html">Expand a log and keep another window open</a><a href="certificates.html">Keep certificates with equipment</a><a href="assetdetails.html">Open asset details and photographs</a><a href="assetlabels.html">Print and scan inventory QR labels</a><a href="assetcalendar.html">Use the linked project calendar</a><a href="lowstock.html">Set low-stock alerts</a><a href="qrverification.html">Scan labels during stock verification</a><a href="fleet.html">Manage vessels and shore bases</a><a href="fleetaccess.html">Set vessel-only access</a><a href="manifests.html">Dispatch and receive with manifests</a><a href="receiving.html">Receive equipment and record final placement</a><a href="itemjourney.html">Follow an item’s journey</a><a href="vessellogs.html">Use vessel-specific logbooks</a><a href="vessellogaccess.html">Set vessel log permissions</a><a href="browseradmin.html">Browser administration and navigation</a><a href="accessreview.html">Review effective access and sensitive backups</a><a href="browsertemplates.html">Browser checklist and maintenance authoring</a><a href="browsertoolbox.html">Browser toolbox-talk form authoring</a><a href="browserlogs.html">Design logbooks in the browser</a></details><a href="handovers.html">Handovers: private drafts and revisions</a><a href="handovercontinuity.html">Prepare handovers &amp; current recipients</a></nav><div class="content"><section class="chapter" data-topic="inventorybuilder" id="inventorybuilder"><p class="kicker">User instructions</p><h1>Build an inventory</h1><p><strong>Import document items into one inventory.</strong> Choose a workbook from Setup &amp; builders, select the item worksheets, then review each mapping and its location. All selected sheets save into one new inventory. To add items to a saved inventory, choose Add to existing inventory or use its Import items action. Check again after changing included sheets, mapped rows, locations or the destination. Browsing another worksheet keeps the completed check. Builder, inventory-view and item-edit permissions are needed to add items.</p><p class="subtitle">Create the structure before entering stock</p><h2>Browser inventory builder</h2>
 <p>Use <strong>Inventory &amp; boxes → Create inventory / Import existing</strong>, or <strong>Setup &amp; builders → Inventory structure</strong>. Creation defines an empty list and locations. Import existing reviews a supported .ajinventory package before saving; document item imports use the separate <strong>Import a document</strong> flow above.</p>
-<p>Browser creation and package import require <strong>Build and import inventory structures</strong> and its inventory dependency. Adding document items to an existing inventory also needs inventory-view and item-edit permissions. An administrator can grant these capabilities to a Technician or Supervisor without changing that person’s role.</p><h2>Native Windows inventory builder (separate workflow)</h2><ol><li>As an administrator, open <strong>Inventory → List setup → Inventory Builder</strong>. Enter the list name and purpose.</li><li>Add storage locations, one per line. Unassigned and In use are supplied automatically. Department custody uses existing project departments; manage those under Departments.</li><li>Add optional fields only when needed. Available types are text, number, date and dropdown choice. Item name, model, serial, part number, asset, quantity, dates, department and location are already included.</li><li>Review and select <strong>Create inventory</strong>. This saves an empty list, not an imported stock count. Add items or import a prepared inventory package separately.</li></ol><p>Back and Next retain changes inside the open wizard. Nothing is saved until Create inventory. Cancel asks before discarding unsaved builder changes. Additional-field structure is fixed after creation; locations can be added later through Locations.</p><h3>Permissions</h3><p>Browser build/import capabilities and operational inventory permissions are separate. Under Users &amp; access → Permissions, control View inventory, Add and edit items, Move items, Run stock verifications and Export reports individually. The native Admin workflow remains available separately. Users with explicitly restricted settings need the relevant capability granted before using it.</p><p>By default, technicians can view inventory and check stock; supervisors can also add/edit and move items. Administrators have full access. Department membership is not a substitute for an application permission.</p><div class="topic-links"><a href="inventory.html">← Find and move inventory</a><a href="stocktake.html">Stock verification →</a></div></section><section class="chapter" id="ui107-retained-inventory-guidance"><h2>1.34.15 — record editing and shipment preparation</h2><p>Inventory item editing now uses <b>Identity → Details &amp; source → Storage &amp; department → Review</b>. Existing item IDs, custom fields, source evidence and version checks remain. Asset notes/low-stock settings have a separate three-page review. Unknown quantity is not zero and an alert does not change stock.</p><p><b>New manifest</b> uses Route, Items &amp; boxes, Transport and Review. Browse origin boxes, then explicitly add records to the <b>Packing selection</b>. Native wide windows show selection beside stock; compact windows stack the panes. Browser checkboxes retain packing across search and box navigation; candidates are paged at 60. Selecting a parent includes its contents once. Changing origin requires confirmation before clearing packing.</p><p>Review route, transport details and grouped contents before <b>Save draft</b>. Preparation is not dispatch. Use separate storage-movement and manifest lifecycle actions for physical events. Back keeps entries and resets confirmation. Existing browser item/profile local forms remain; native and Fleet forms are memory-only, not a durable queue. See user-guide pages 133–136. Existing 1.34.11 training examples remain compatible.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui107-boxes-and-contents"><h2>Review boxes and their contents before import</h2><p>After mapping an inventory worksheet, open <strong>Boxes and contents</strong>. Review each included row's asset/tag reference, explicit box flag, parent box reference and expected quantity. Searching, paging and opening this view do not change the checked proposal. Editing a field requires checking the changed draft again.</p><p>A parent must be an included, explicitly marked box with a unique asset/tag reference in the <strong>same worksheet</strong>. Use its exact reference, including leading zeros and punctuation, or choose <strong>No container</strong> deliberately. A name, serial number, part number, indentation or the word BOX does not establish a relationship. References across worksheets or to boxes already in the destination inventory are not resolved during this import.</p><p>Review missing or excluded parents, duplicate references, self-links, cycles and excessive depth. A box describes one container; use an expected quantity of one or leave it Unknown when appropriate. Ordinary stock can have zero or another valid expected quantity. No imported quantity is a completed stock verification.</p><p>Contained rows inherit their top box's effective location. The checked import summary uses that location before saving, and a differing mapped location is retained in Notes. Review this together with worksheet locations. A location note records the reviewed mapping; it is not proof of a physical move.</p><p>Explicit parent and box-flag headers help suggest inventory. Unqualified Box/Container ID or reference headers can identify the row itself or its parent, so map them deliberately as an asset/tag or parent reference. Unmapped source columns remain available as source notes.</p><p>Field edits keep full mapped row order, original row references when available and item choices. Reapplying a mapping replaces the mapped values and these corrections; editing the complete table can reset source references and choices. Review the visible notice before continuing. Pending or uncertain saves must retain their unchanged retry request.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui108-inventory-source-review"><h2>Review source rows and header choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, use <strong>Needs source review</strong> to inspect rows that resemble repeated headers, headings, summaries, instructions or footers. The advice describes the original extracted source. Rows remain included until you deliberately exclude them. Items can legitimately be called Total or Instructions; compare their identifiers and expected quantities with the source.</p><p>The header selector includes the first 250 extracted nonempty rows. Open <strong>Find header row</strong> to search and page through any extracted row, compare its preview, and choose the actual column header. Original Excel row labels appear only when the extractor proves them. Review any notice about rows before the selected header or other header candidates. Changing the header requires applying the mapping and checking the changed proposal again.</p><p>Editing the complete raw table clears source-row advice and provenance when they can no longer be established. Field corrections keep their original-source references, but do not turn the original advice into a statement about the corrected item. Source Counted columns remain Notes; the app performs stock verification.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="ui109-inventory-item-corrections"><h2>Correct one imported item without resetting choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, open <strong>Edit item</strong> to correct that row's <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Serial number (SN)</strong> or <strong>Part number (PN)</strong>. Apply a real change, then <strong>Check</strong> the proposal again. Cancel or an unchanged Apply retains the existing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships.</p><p>Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains.</p></section><footer class="topic