. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal.</p><p id="ui112-inventory-review-navigation"><strong>Navigate the inventory review.</strong> <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> and each worksheet’s <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> button change only the sheet on screen. <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping.</p><p id="ui113-inventory-mapping-recovery"><strong>Undo pending mapping choices without replacing corrected rows.</strong> <strong>Restore last applied mapping</strong> restores the recorded header and column choices for the worksheet you are inspecting. Current item edits, full Notes, row exclusions, source references and box relationships stay in place. The pending changes show which destination fields or header were changed. Restoration does not apply source values to the rows and requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving. <strong>Apply mapping to rows</strong> still replaces mapped values and asks before replacing deliberate corrections. The restore action is unavailable if this draft has no recorded last-applied mapping; older drafts are not guessed from their item rows. Busy or uncertain saves remain locked; resolve an uncertain result with the unchanged retry.</p><p id="ui114-inventory-worksheet-overview"><strong>Review mapping across worksheets.</strong> Each card in <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows its current mapping status and row choices. The summary names included worksheets with pending mapping and separates missing-name or unavailable-choice advice. <strong>All worksheets</strong>, <strong>Included</strong> and <strong>Needs mapping</strong> only filter the cards on screen; they do not add or exclude worksheets, switch the worksheet being inspected, or change a completed check and confirmation. Needs mapping can show excluded worksheets too. Their advice does not require adding them to the import. Use <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> to inspect a specific worksheet. Apply or restore pending mappings on included worksheets before checking again. A missing source name column is mapping advice; manually edited rows still need comparison with the source and a fresh check. An older draft without a recorded applied mapping remains explicitly unavailable for restoration.</p><p id="ui115-inventory-worksheet-overlap"><strong>Review possible overlap across worksheets.</strong> Open <strong>Review possible overlap</strong> to compare exact matching serial numbers (SN) or asset references in included rows from different included worksheets. Each match remains a separate record. Locations and part numbers provide context; matching part numbers or names alone do not identify overlap. Leading zeros and letter case remain significant. These suggestions are not a stock verification or a duplicate verdict. Excluded worksheets and rows are outside this comparison, and items with neither identifier cannot be compared. Pending mapping choices have not changed the displayed rows. Full mapped-row editing can make the original source row unavailable. Use <strong>Inspect items</strong> to review the current worksheet, or <strong>Inspect source row</strong> where a unique original Excel row is available. These controls preserve a completed check and confirmation. Review the original file when source provenance is unavailable. No rows are merged, removed or excluded automatically. If you edit the proposal, use <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving.</p><p id="ui116-inventory-source-headers"><strong>Review source table headers.</strong> Open <strong>Review source table headers</strong> beside the source browser to inspect possible headers in the first 5,000 extracted rows of the current worksheet. Compare each candidate with all 13 recorded last-applied mapping choices. The original column heading and the candidate text at that same column are shown together. Recognized alternative headings, changed positions, missing headings and repeated aliases are suggestions to review against the source. A candidate is not proof of a new table or a correct mapping. Pending choices are not used as an applied mapping, and missing recorded choices remain explicitly unavailable. Full mapped-row edits may differ from the earlier applied source mapping. <strong>Inspect source row</strong> opens the exact extracted row. <strong>Inspect mapped item</strong> is available only when a unique confirmed original Excel row still links to that item. These actions preserve your checked proposal and confirmation. This view does not combine tables, change the header or mapping, remove rows, or estimate table boundaries. Use the existing header chooser and Apply controls for deliberate mapping changes, then check the draft again. No candidates does not prove the worksheet has one consistent layout; review the complete file for merged, adjacent or unrecognized tables.</p></main></body></html>--- a/tests/test_inventory_source_headers_ui116.js
